CORE
main.c
--dependence-graph --show
activate-multi-line-match
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
\/\/ ([0-9]+).*\n.*p := address_of\(x\)\n(.*\n)*Data dependencies: ([0-9]+,)*\1(,[0-9]+)*\n\n.*\n.*HAVOC_REACHABLE \(arbitrary memory\)
\/\/ ([0-9]+).*\n.*HAVOC_REACHABLE \(arbitrary memory\)\n(.*\n)*Data dependencies: ([0-9]+,)*\1(,[0-9]+)*\n\n.*\n.*out := \*p
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The havoc_reachable statement emitted for the inline assembly reads the
pointers stored in the objects reachable from the objects of static lifetime
(here, p), and writes the objects it reaches (here, x, which out is then read
from).
